# g96-screen-viewer: core wire

No hot file needs text for this task: it adds no protocol method, no module line (the new module is declared inside
`compose_screen.rs`: `pub(crate) mod live;` over `compose_screen_live.rs`; `mixdog-remote` gets `pub mod screen;` in its own
`webrtc/mod.rs`), no Cargo dependency edge (the daemon already depends on mixdog-remote, mixdog-tools, bytes and futures; mixdog-remote
already has jpeg-decoder, base64, regex, tokio and futures) and no change to `compose_flip.rs`.

What the wiring should know:

1. `LiveViewService::bind_screens(phone)` (called by compose_flip.rs where `live_view.bind_screens(phone)` is) now also builds the
   live view's screens and hands the sessions' sink to the screen service (`PhoneScreens::attach`). The trait gained `resolve`,
   `capture`, `attach` and `grant` is async. Nothing else implements `PhoneScreens` in the tree.
2. SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs): no name of this task's is listed there; nothing to remove.
3. Delete item 1 of the "Open, no owner yet" list of deferred-g95.md (the Rust screen viewer, the display list before a granted
   client's ready) once this commit is merged. Item 8 of that list (the dead arm "host/screen/displays" in
   mixdog-app-server/src/tests/inventory_rule.rs) is not this task's: it goes with the rows of g9-screen-switch that remove
   host/screen/displays (a file of mixdog-app-server, not owned here).
4. Not done here, for a later task (files of g85-fu-computer, not owned): one `InputDesktop` type. `computer_screen_input::InputDesktop`
   {name, consent, logon_ui} and `screen_source::InputDesktop` {input_desktop, consent, logon_ui} are still two, joined by
   `input_desktop()` in compose_screen_service.rs. To unify: `screen_source` re-exports the computer_screen_input type (with
   `secure_up`), its field `input_desktop` becomes `name`, and `session.rs` (`host.desktop()?.input_desktop` -> `.name`),
   `computer_screen_source.rs` `local_desktop` and its test fake follow; `input_desktop()` and its test in compose_screen_service*.rs are
   then deleted.
5. Rate of the picture (a gap to close before the Electron screen sources go): `ScreenSources::capture` takes the desktop's own capture
   (`host/computer/pixels`, a JPEG of at most 1920 px read back from the blob store, one every 100 ms plus the request) because the
   in-process capture is of the whole virtual screen, where Electron's desktopCapturer track ran at the plan's 30 fps at full size.
   A per-monitor in-process capture (`ComputerBackend::screen_source(display)` for one monitor of `host/computer/displays`) or a desktop
   that streams its frames would remove it; both are outside this task's files.
